    "editorial_evidence": [
      "Pinned WLC 2 Kings 14:13 first Jehoash o120140130061 = father of Amaziah (Judah); second o120140130101 = Jehoash king of Israel; verbs o120140130162, o120140130182, 14:14 o120140140012, o120140140182 follow Israelite king",
      "Pinned WLC 2 Chronicles 25:23 first Joash o140250230061 = father of Amaziah; second o140250230101 = king of Israel; verbs o140250230152, o140250230172, 25:24 o140250240202 follow Israelite king",
      "Clear-Bible/macula-hebrew@47db250bd55d0d8577f2a94fba114ef16c35b23c WLC/lowfat/12-2Ki-014-lowfat.xml and WLC/lowfat/14-2Ch-025-lowfat.xml",
      "https://biblehub.com/2_kings/14-13.htm",
      "https://biblehub.com/2_chronicles/25-23.htm"
    ],
    "editorial_reason": "2 Kings 14:13 and 2 Chronicles 25:23 each mention two kings named Joash: the first name is Amaziah's father Joash of Judah, the second is the capturing Joash/Jehoash of Israel. The source assigned the two exact explicit Hebrew words to the opposite men and additionally attributed seven singular action-verbs of the Israelite king to the deceased king of Judah. Correct only these two exact name groups and seven role pointers; preserve both historically distinct kings and all original source files and verse references.",
    "review_status": "editorially_reviewed",
